%% Hopline — Direct mode: two desktop apps hand off a file from the WebRTC data channel to a native TCP link.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant SP as Sender page (renderer)
  participant SM as Sender main process
  participant RM as Receiver main process
  participant RP as Receiver page (renderer)

  Note over SP,RP: Paired over WebRTC as usual. The data channel is DTLS-encrypted and the safety code authenticates it
  SP->>RP: sync { v: 3, direct: true, ... }
  RP->>SP: sync { v: 3, direct: true, ... }
  SP->>RP: offer { batchId, files }
  Note over RP: User clicks Accept (Downloads/Hopline date)<br/>or Save to a folder (native dialog) → folder id
  RP->>SP: answer { batchId, accept: true }

  Note over SP: File picked from disk: preload turns it into a token<br/>(webUtils.getPathForFile, never a path in the page)
  SP->>RP: direct-request { id }
  RP->>RM: listen() + expect { id, folderId, path, size }
  Note over RM: TCP listener on 0.0.0.0, random port (IPv4 only)<br/>fresh random 256-bit key per listener
  RM-->>RP: { port, addresses, key }
  RP->>SP: direct-ready { id, ok: true, link: { port, addresses, key } }
  Note over SP,RP: The key travels only over the authenticated data channel, never via the signaling server

  SP->>SM: connect(link)
  Note over SM: Keeps own-subnet or 100.64/10 addresses only<br/>loopback only if the receiver lists one of our own addresses
  SM->>RM: TCP connect (all targets at once, 3 s timeout)
  SM->>RM: 🔒 HELLO { v: 1 } (AES-256-GCM, counter nonce 0)
  alt Wrong key, junk or too slow
    RM--xSM: socket closed (hard 10 s deadline, max 8 pending, max 2 per address)
  else Key proven
    Note over RM: Accepts exactly ONE authenticated connection,<br/>then stops listening and drops other pending sockets
    RM->>SM: 🔒 READY
  end

  SP->>SM: send { id, fileToken, size }
  SM->>RM: 🔒 FILE { id, size }
  Note over RM: Only an expected id at exactly that size<br/>SafeFileWriter opens an exclusive .hopline-part temp file
  loop Until the whole file is sent
    SM->>RM: 🔒 CHUNK (≤ 512 KiB, with backpressure)
    RM-->>SM: 🔒 PROGRESS { id, bytes } (every 8 MiB written)
  end
  SM->>RM: 🔒 END { sha256 }
  Note over RM: SHA-256 compared (timingSafeEqual) BEFORE commit<br/>commit never overwrites, no symlinks
  RM->>SM: 🔒 RESULT { id, ok: true }
  RM-->>RP: received { id, ok, savedAs (relative) }
  SM-->>SP: { ok: true }

  opt Receiver cancels, or its disk fails
    RM->>SM: 🔒 SKIP { id, error? }
    SM->>RM: 🔒 ABORT { id }
  end

  alt No direct-ready within 10 s, ok false, or not reachable
    SP->>RP: start { id, offset: 0, slot } over WebRTC
    Note over RP: The start cancels the Direct expectation for this file
  else Link lost, or no progress for 20 s (stall watchdog)
    Note over RM: Partial file deleted, row back to queued
    SP->>RP: start { id, offset: 0, slot } over WebRTC (Direct mode off for this session)
    Note over RP: If the file was already saved, progress + ack are repeated instead
  end
